# Safety, Authorization, and Recovery — {{TITLE}}

## Default boundary

- Use owned or explicitly authorized systems and data.
- Prefer simulators, containers, fixtures, mock services, synthetic data, and disposable targets.
- Start with read-only observation.
- Prefer temporary and reversible changes over persistent ones.
- Never use a production system or daily-use device as the first target.

## Before a persistent or risky change

- [ ] Exact target and scope are recorded.
- [ ] Current state and version are captured.
- [ ] Important data is backed up and restoration is understood.
- [ ] Recovery artifact or clean baseline matches the target.
- [ ] Recovery procedure has been tested at the relevant level.
- [ ] Stop conditions are explicit.
- [ ] Power, storage, connectivity, and supervision needs are satisfied.
- [ ] Authorization and downstream impact are confirmed.

## Recovery record

| Field | Value | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Target |  |  |
| Baseline state |  |  |
| Backup |  |  |
| Recovery method |  |  |
| Recovery test result | Not tested |  |
| Residual risk |  |  |

An untested recovery plan is not recovery evidence.
